; a missing file after that is limit reached; never persist an unreadable flag); the policy file and any override variable are ignored outside the signed test marker (also under the temp dir); SAFE_SWARM patterns anchored at both ends and every segment of a compound command tested; ssh and git config files under the home directory stay protected from session writes. (3) Add a short 'Parked: git actions under policy' section to docs/plans/ideas.md listing that git auto-approve needs a dedicated review (pinned git, atomic checks in one process, protect the git common dir, push by literal URL and explicit refspec, staged-file check, cwd equals root) before it returns. (4) Update docs/auto-approve.md accordingly (files only, no git). Keep the orchestrator-mode, handbuild, guard, self-approval, completion and swarm-merge tests passing.",
